   'rounds_reps',
   'Dominic J. Hall honors Dominic J. Hall, 33, who served in the U.S. Marine Corps with 3rd Force Recon Company in Afghanistan and in the Army Special Forces with Bravo Company, 2nd Battalion, 19th Special Forces Group. He was also a police officer with the Appleton Police Department in Wisconsin. He died on Sept. 4, 2022, of pancreatic cancer deemed a direct result of his service during the Global War on Terror.

The workout runs on one 48-minute clock while you wear a vest (20 lb / 14 lb). For the first 12:23 you do as many box step-ups (20 in) as you can. You rest until 15:00, then do as many rounds as possible of 9 deadlifts (275 lb / 185 lb), a 400 m run and 22 push-ups until 48:00. The step-ups tire your legs before 33 minutes of heavy pulling and running.',
   '[{"name": "Box Step-Ups", "reps": "Max reps, 0:00–12:23", "tip": "Wear the vest. Stand all the way up on the box and switch legs each rep to share the work.", "rx_men": "20 in, 20 lb vest", "rx_women": "20 in, 14 lb vest"}, {"name": "Rest", "reps": "12:23–15:00", "isRest": true, "tip": "Drink some water and load the deadlift bar."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "9", "tip": "Flat back and the bar close to your legs. Quick singles are fine at this load.", "rx_men": "275 lb", "rx_women": "185 lb"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Hold a pace you can repeat every round for 33 minutes."}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "22", "tip": "Chest to the floor and arms locked at the top. Break into sets before you fail."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record two scores: total box step-ups from 0:00 to 12:23, and rounds + reps from 15:00 to 48:00. CrossFit does not say whether to combine them.',
   '["Pace the step-ups so your legs are ready for the deadlifts", "Use the rest to set up the bar", "Steady runs beat fast first rounds"]'::jsonb,
   '["Find a step-up rhythm you can hold for the full 12:23 rather than sprinting the first few minutes.", "CrossFit lists the vest with the loads and does not say to take it off for the second part, so plan to wear it for the full 48 minutes.", "On the deadlifts, set your back before every rep and reset at the floor instead of bouncing the bar.", "Break the push-ups into sets early, such as 8, 7 and 7, so the run stays a run.", "Use a counter or a whiteboard for both parts so both scores are accurate."]'::jsonb,
   'Drop the vest or use a lighter one, and use a lower box for the step-ups. Lower the deadlifts to 185 lb / 125 lb, or to a load you can lift for fast singles while tired. Do push-ups from the knees or with your hands on a bench, and shorten the run to 200 m if 400 m takes more than about 3 minutes.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Dominic J. Hall workout?", "answer": "On a running clock, wearing a vest (20 lb / 14 lb): max box step-ups (20 in) from 0:00 to 12:23, rest until 15:00, then as many rounds as possible until 48:00 of 9 deadlifts (275 lb / 185 lb), a 400 m run and 22 push-ups."}, {"question": "How is Dominic J. Hall scored?", "answer": "Record your total step-ups and your rounds plus reps in the 33-minute AMRAP. CrossFit does not say whether to add them together, so keep them as two scores."}, {"question": "Do I wear the vest for the whole workout?", "answer": "CrossFit lists the vest with the loads without saying when to take it off, so most athletes wear it for all 48 minutes. Scale it if you need to."}, {"question": "Who was Dominic J. Hall?", "answer": "A U.S. Marine Corps and Army Special Forces veteran and Appleton, Wisconsin, police officer. He died at 33 on Sept. 4, 2022, of pancreatic cancer deemed a direct result of his service during the Global War on Terror."}]'::jsonb,
