   'Donny honors U.S. Army Spc. Donald L. Nichols, 21, of Shell Rock, Iowa, of the 1st Battalion, 133rd Infantry Regiment, Iowa Army National Guard, based in Waterloo, Iowa. He died on April 13, 2011, in Laghman Province, Afghanistan, of wounds suffered when insurgents attacked his unit with an improvised explosive device.

You alternate deadlifts (225 lb / 155 lb) and burpees in sets of 21, 15, 9, 9, 15 and 21. That is 90 deadlifts and 90 burpees. Most ladders get easier as they go, but this one climbs back up, so the biggest sets come at the end when your back and lungs are already tired.',
   '[{"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "21-15-9-9-15-21", "tip": "Flat back and the bar close to your legs. Break the big sets early, such as 7, 7 and 7.", "rx_men": "225 lb", "rx_women": "155 lb"}, {"name": "Burpees", "reps": "21-15-9-9-15-21", "tip": "Chest to the floor and a small jump at the top. Find a steady rhythm and keep moving."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Save energy for the last round of 21", "Small deadlift sets protect your back", "Move straight from the bar to the burpees"]'::jsonb,
   '["Treat the first 21 as a warm-up pace, because you have to do it again at the end.", "Use a hook grip or mixed grip so your hands do not limit the deadlifts.", "Reset your back at the floor on every rep once you get tired, rather than bouncing the bar.", "On the burpees, step back and step up if jumping makes you stop to rest.", "Keep your rests short and planned, such as five breaths between deadlift sets."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the deadlifts to 155 lb / 105 lb, or to a load you can lift in sets of 7 while tired. Do step-back burpees without the jump, or cut the ladder to 15-9-6-6-9-15 if the full version would take more than about 25 minutes.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Donny workout?", "answer": "21-15-9-9-15-21 reps for time of deadlifts (225 lb / 155 lb) and burpees."}, {"question": "How many reps are in Donny?", "answer": "90 deadlifts and 90 burpees, 180 reps in all."}, {"question": "Who was Donny?", "answer": "U.S. Army Spc. Donald L. Nichols, 21, of Shell Rock, Iowa, of the Iowa Army National Guard. He died on April 13, 2011, in Laghman Province, Afghanistan, after an improvised explosive device attack on his unit."}, {"question": "What is the hardest part of Donny?", "answer": "The final round of 21. The ladder climbs back up, so you meet the biggest sets when you are most tired."}]'::jsonb,
