   'Dragon honors U.S. Army Capt. Nicholas Rozanski, 36, of Dublin, Ohio, of the 1st Battalion, 148th Infantry Regiment, 37th Infantry Brigade Combat Team, Ohio National Guard, based in Walbridge, Ohio. He died on April 4, 2012, of wounds sustained during an enemy attack in Faryab province, Afghanistan.

The workout is a 5K run, then 4 minutes to find your heaviest set of 4 deadlifts, then a second 5K run, then 4 minutes to find your heaviest set of 4 push jerks. That is 10 km of running with two heavy lifts in between. Lifting heavy straight after a long run, and running again on tired legs, is what makes it hard.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "5 km", "tip": "Start at a pace you could hold for a 10K. You still have another 5K to go."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "4-rep max in 4 min", "tip": "Have plates ready before you start. Make two or three jumps in weight, not five."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "5 km", "tip": "Your legs will feel heavy for the first kilometer. Settle in and hold your pace."}, {"name": "Push Jerks", "reps": "4-rep max in 4 min", "tip": "Dip straight down and drive hard. Lock out each rep overhead before the next."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time, plus your 4-rep-max deadlift and push jerk. CrossFit does not say how to combine them.',
   '["Run the first 5K easier than you want to", "Plan your lifting jumps before you start", "Stay warm between the lifts and the second run"]'::jsonb,
   '["Load the bar near your working weight before the first run so you only add plates during the 4 minutes.", "Plan two or three deadlift attempts, such as 70, 80 and 90 percent of a fresh 4-rep max, since your legs will not be fresh.", "Keep a flat back on every deadlift. A slightly lighter lift with good form is better than a heavy one that rounds.", "On the push jerks, keep your elbows high in the rack and push yourself under the bar as you lock out.", "Most athletes leave the clock running during the 4-minute lifting windows, so your time is the full workout from start to finish."]'::jsonb,
   'Shorten each run to 3 km or 2 km, or row 5,000 m in place of a run. Keep the lifts, but work up to a heavy set of 4 you can do with clean form rather than a true max. Use push presses instead of push jerks if the dip and drive are new to you.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Dragon workout?", "answer": "For time: run 5K, take 4 minutes to find a 4-rep-max deadlift, run 5K, then take 4 minutes to find a 4-rep-max push jerk."}, {"question": "How is Dragon scored?", "answer": "CrossFit lists it as for time. Most athletes record the total time and the two lifts. CrossFit does not say how to combine them."}, {"question": "Who was Dragon?", "answer": "U.S. Army Capt. Nicholas Rozanski, 36, of Dublin, Ohio, of the Ohio National Guard. He died on April 4, 2012, of wounds sustained during an enemy attack in Faryab province, Afghanistan."}, {"question": "How long does Dragon take?", "answer": "Most athletes finish in about 50 to 75 minutes, depending on 5K pace, since the two lifting windows add 8 minutes."}]'::jsonb,
