   'time',
   'Drew honors Chief Warrant Officer 3 Andrew "Drew" Gunnison Cully, 35, of Ozark, Missouri, an instructor pilot with C Company, 4th Battalion, 160th Special Operations Aviation Regiment, the "Night Stalkers." He died on Sept. 17, 2025, when his MH-60M Black Hawk crashed during a training mission near Joint Base Lewis-McChord, Washington.

Each of the four rounds is named for one of the heroes who died in the crash: Kraus, Scott, Good and Cully. The runs grow from 200 m to 800 m while the pull-ups and hand-release push-ups drop from 30 to 15, and every round ends with 4 deadlifts at 1.5 times your bodyweight. You rest 30 seconds between rounds, then finish with 269 step-ups, the Night Stalkers round, all while wearing a vest.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "200 m", "tip": "Kraus round. Start easy. The vest makes every run harder than it looks."}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "30", "tip": "Chin over the bar. Break into small sets from the start."}, {"name": "Hand-Release Push-Ups", "reps": "30", "tip": "Chest to the floor and lift your hands at the bottom of every rep."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "4", "tip": "Set your back before each rep. Singles are fine at this load.", "rx_men": "1.5x bodyweight", "rx_women": "1.5x bodyweight"}, {"name": "Rest", "reps": "30 sec", "isRest": true, "tip": "Shake out your arms and get to the start line."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Scott round. Settle into a pace you can repeat."}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "25", "tip": "Keep sets small and rests short."}, {"name": "Hand-Release Push-Ups", "reps": "25", "tip": "Rest at the top, not lying on the floor."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "4", "tip": "Same load each round. Reset at the floor.", "rx_men": "1.5x bodyweight", "rx_women": "1.5x bodyweight"}, {"name": "Rest", "reps": "30 sec", "isRest": true, "tip": "Breathe and get ready to run."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "600 m", "tip": "Good round. Use the longer run to let your arms recover."}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "20", "tip": "Sets of 4 or 5 keep you moving."}, {"name": "Hand-Release Push-Ups", "reps": "20", "tip": "Keep your body in a straight line."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "4", "tip": "Flat back, bar close to your legs.", "rx_men": "1.5x bodyweight", "rx_women": "1.5x bodyweight"}, {"name": "Rest", "reps": "30 sec", "isRest": true, "tip": "Last rest. The longest run is next."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Cully round. Hold your pace."}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "15", "tip": "Chin over the bar on every rep."}, {"name": "Hand-Release Push-Ups", "reps": "15", "tip": "Short sets and quick rests."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "4", "tip": "Last four heavy pulls. Keep your form.", "rx_men": "1.5x bodyweight", "rx_women": "1.5x bodyweight"}, {"name": "Box Step-Ups", "reps": "269", "tip": "Night Stalkers round. Switch legs each rep and keep a steady rhythm."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Pace the first round, the step-ups come last", "Break pull-ups and push-ups into small sets", "Keep the deadlifts as clean singles"]'::jsonb,
   '["CrossFit says to wear a weight vest but does not give a weight, a box height for the step-ups, or whether the clock stops during the 30-second rests. Decide these before you start and write them down with your score.", "Many athletes use a 20 lb / 14 lb vest, which is the usual Hero WOD standard, but that is a gym choice rather than CrossFit''s rule.", "Work out 1.5 times your bodyweight before you start and load the bar once so you never change plates.", "Break the 30 pull-ups and 30 push-ups of the first round into small sets so the later rounds stay steady.", "On the 269 step-ups, count in blocks of 10 or 20 and switch legs on every rep."]'::jsonb,
   'Drop the vest or use a lighter one. Lower the deadlifts to bodyweight or less, and use a lower box for the step-ups. Replace pull-ups with jumping pull-ups or ring rows, and do hand-release push-ups from the knees. Halve the pull-ups and push-ups in each round, or cut the step-ups to 135, if the full version would take more than about 75 minutes.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Drew workout?", "answer": "For time, in a vest: Kraus, 200 m run, 30 pull-ups, 30 hand-release push-ups, 4 deadlifts; Scott, 400 m, 25, 25, 4; Good, 600 m, 20, 20, 4; Cully, 800 m, 15, 15, 4; then Night Stalkers, 269 step-ups. Rest 30 seconds between the first four rounds. Deadlifts are 1.5 times bodyweight."}, {"question": "How many reps are in Drew?", "answer": "2,000 m of running, 90 pull-ups, 90 hand-release push-ups, 16 deadlifts and 269 step-ups."}, {"question": "What vest weight and box height does Drew use?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Many gyms use a 20 lb / 14 lb vest and a 20 in box, but record what you used."}, {"question": "Who was Drew?", "answer": "Chief Warrant Officer 3 Andrew \"Drew\" Gunnison Cully, 35, of Ozark, Missouri, of the 160th Special Operations Aviation Regiment. He died on Sept. 17, 2025, when his MH-60M Black Hawk crashed during a training mission near Joint Base Lewis-McChord, Washington."}]'::jsonb,
