   'Dunn honors U.S. Marine Corps Lance Cpl. Kielin Dunn, 19, of Chesapeake, Virginia, of the 1st Battalion, 6th Marine Regiment, 2nd Marine Division, II Marine Expeditionary Force, at Camp Lejeune, North Carolina. He died on Feb. 18, 2010, while supporting combat operations in Helmand Province, Afghanistan. His friends remember his passion for CrossFit and break dancing.

You get 19 minutes to complete as many rounds as possible of 3 muscle-ups, one shuttle sprint to 5, 10 and 15 yards, and 6 burpee box jump-overs (20 in). The muscle-up sets are small, but they come back fast, and the sprint and burpees keep your heart rate high the whole time.',
   '[{"name": "Muscle-Ups", "reps": "3", "tip": "Do all three as one set if you can, or as quick singles."}, {"name": "Shuttle Sprints", "reps": "5, 10, 15 yd", "tip": "Touch each line with your hand and change direction low and fast."}, {"name": "Burpee Box Jump-Over", "reps": "6", "tip": "Jump over the box without touching it, as CrossFit''s standard says.", "rx_men": "20 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total rounds + reps.',
   '["Keep the muscle-ups smooth and unbroken", "Sprint hard but stay under control on the turns", "Find a burpee rhythm you can hold"]'::jsonb,
   '["CrossFit does not mark out the shuttle sprint, and most gyms run it out and back to 5, 10 and 15 yards, for 60 yards in all.", "On the burpee box jump-overs, CrossFit says you must clear the box without touching it, so jump a little higher than you think you need to.", "Chalk before each set of muscle-ups and use a strong hip drive to save your arms.", "Walk the few steps back to the rings to catch your breath, then go straight into the next set.", "Count your rounds on a whiteboard so your score is accurate."]'::jsonb,
   'Replace each muscle-up with 2 pull-ups plus 2 ring dips, or do banded muscle-up transitions. Jog the shuttle instead of sprinting. Use a lower box, or step over it after each burpee, if jumping over without touching is not safe for you yet.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Dunn workout?", "answer": "As many rounds as possible in 19 minutes of 3 muscle-ups, 1 shuttle sprint (5, 10 and 15 yards) and 6 burpee box jump-overs (20 in)."}, {"question": "How is the shuttle sprint done in Dunn?", "answer": "CrossFit lists 5, 10 and 15 yards without more detail. Most athletes run out and back to each line, for 60 yards per round."}, {"question": "Who was Dunn?", "answer": "U.S. Marine Corps Lance Cpl. Kielin Dunn, 19, of Chesapeake, Virginia, of the 1st Battalion, 6th Marine Regiment. He died on Feb. 18, 2010, while supporting combat operations in Helmand Province, Afghanistan."}, {"question": "Can I touch the box on the burpee jump-overs?", "answer": "No. CrossFit''s version says to jump over the box without touching it."}]'::jsonb,
