   'DVB honors Officer David Vanbuskirk, 36, of Henderson, Nevada, who joined the Las Vegas Metropolitan Police Department in 1999 and its Search and Rescue Team in 2007. He was killed on July 23, 2013, when he fell during a nighttime aerial rescue mission in Las Vegas.

You run a mile carrying a medicine ball (20 lb / 14 lb), then do 8 rounds of 10 wall-ball shots and 1 rope climb. Then you run 800 m with the ball and do 4 rounds, then 400 m and 2 rounds. That adds up to 140 wall balls, 14 rope climbs and about 2.8 km of running with the ball. The ball carry wears out your arms and grip before every climb.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "1 mile", "tip": "Carry the medicine ball the whole way. Switch how you hold it to rest your arms.", "rx_men": "20 lb ball", "rx_women": "14 lb ball"}, {"name": "Wall Balls", "reps": "8 rounds of 10", "tip": "Full squat and hit the target every rep.", "rx_men": "20 lb, 10 ft", "rx_women": "14 lb, 9 ft"}, {"name": "Rope Climbs", "reps": "8 rounds of 1", "tip": "Use a foot lock to save your arms. Come down under control."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Carry the medicine ball again. Keep a steady pace.", "rx_men": "20 lb ball", "rx_women": "14 lb ball"}, {"name": "Wall Balls", "reps": "4 rounds of 10", "tip": "Unbroken sets of 10 if you can.", "rx_men": "20 lb, 10 ft", "rx_women": "14 lb, 9 ft"}, {"name": "Rope Climbs", "reps": "4 rounds of 1", "tip": "Chalk up before each climb."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Last run with the ball.", "rx_men": "20 lb ball", "rx_women": "14 lb ball"}, {"name": "Wall Balls", "reps": "2 rounds of 10", "tip": "Finish strong but keep hitting the target.", "rx_men": "20 lb, 10 ft", "rx_women": "14 lb, 9 ft"}, {"name": "Rope Climbs", "reps": "2 rounds of 1", "tip": "Last two climbs. Foot lock every time."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Hold the ball at your chest and keep your arms relaxed on the runs", "Foot lock every rope climb", "Unbroken sets of 10 wall balls save time"]'::jsonb,
   '["CrossFit does not give a rope climb height. Most gyms use 15 feet, so record what you used.", "On the runs, hug the ball at your chest or carry it on one shoulder and switch sides when your arms tire.", "Keep each set of 10 wall balls unbroken if you can, since the rope climb gives your legs a short break.", "Use a foot lock on every climb and lower yourself hand over hand rather than sliding.", "Count the rounds of each block on a whiteboard so you do not lose track."]'::jsonb,
   'Use a lighter medicine ball for the runs and wall balls, and a lower target if needed. Replace each rope climb with 3 lying rope pulls to standing or a partial climb. Shorten the first run to 800 m, or cut the 8-round block to 6 rounds, if the full version would take more than about 55 minutes.',
   '[{"question": "What is the DVB workout?", "answer": "For time: run 1 mile with a medicine ball, then 8 rounds of 10 wall-ball shots and 1 rope climb; run 800 m with the ball, then 4 rounds; run 400 m with the ball, then 2 rounds. The ball is 20 lb / 14 lb and the targets are 10 ft / 9 ft."}, {"question": "How many reps are in DVB?", "answer": "140 wall-ball shots, 14 rope climbs and about 2.8 km of running with the medicine ball."}, {"question": "How high is the rope climb in DVB?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Most gyms use a 15-foot rope."}, {"question": "Who was DVB?", "answer": "Officer David Vanbuskirk, 36, of Henderson, Nevada, a member of the Las Vegas Metropolitan Police Department''s Search and Rescue Team. He was killed on July 23, 2013, when he fell during a nighttime aerial rescue mission."}]'::jsonb,
