   'time',
   'Emily honors U.S. Army 2nd Lt. Emily Jazmin Tatum Perez, 23, of the 204th Support Battalion, 2nd Brigade, 4th Infantry Division. She was killed on Sept. 12, 2006, when her Humvee was struck by an improvised explosive device as she led a convoy through Al Kifl, Iraq. A 2005 West Point graduate and track athlete, she was the first female African-American officer in U.S. military history to die in combat.

The workout uses some of her favorite movements. You complete 10 rounds of 30 double-unders, 15 pull-ups, 30 squats and a 100 m sprint, with 2 minutes of rest after each round. That is 300 double-unders, 150 pull-ups and 300 squats. The rest lets you push each round hard, so the sprints should stay fast.',
   '[{"name": "Double-Unders", "reps": "30", "tip": "Stay relaxed, jump a little higher and spin the rope from your wrists."}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "15", "tip": "Chin over the bar. Break into sets of 5 to 8 before your grip goes."}, {"name": "Air Squats", "reps": "30", "tip": "Hips below the knees at the bottom and stand all the way up."}, {"name": "Sprint", "reps": "100 m", "tip": "Run fast. The rest is coming."}, {"name": "Rest", "reps": "2 min", "isRest": true, "tip": "Walk around, breathe and get to the rope."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Use the rest so every sprint stays fast", "Small pull-up sets save your grip", "Keep the double-unders relaxed"]'::jsonb,
   '["CrossFit does not say whether you rest after the tenth round or whether the clock stops during rests. Most athletes keep the clock running and stop it after the last sprint.", "Treat each round as a hard effort, since the 2-minute rest lets your heart rate come down.", "Plan your pull-up sets, such as 8 and 7 or three sets of 5, and keep that plan in later rounds.", "If double-unders start to trip you up, take a short break instead of fighting through misses.", "On the sprint, drive your arms and stay tall."]'::jsonb,
   'Replace double-unders with 60 single-unders or 30 seconds of practice attempts. Use jumping pull-ups or ring rows, or cut the pull-ups to 10 per round. Run the 100 m at a fast but safe pace, and cut to 6 rounds if ten would take more than about an hour.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Emily workout?", "answer": "10 rounds for time of 30 double-unders, 15 pull-ups, 30 squats and a 100 m sprint, with 2 minutes of rest after each round."}, {"question": "How many reps are in Emily?", "answer": "300 double-unders, 150 pull-ups, 300 squats and 1,000 m of sprinting."}, {"question": "Does the clock stop during the rest in Emily?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Most athletes keep the clock running and include the rest in their time, then stop after the last sprint."}, {"question": "Who was Emily?", "answer": "U.S. Army 2nd Lt. Emily Jazmin Tatum Perez, 23, a 2005 West Point graduate. She was killed on Sept. 12, 2006, when her Humvee was struck by an improvised explosive device while she led a convoy through Al Kifl, Iraq."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lH0zsR8CK4E'),
  ('Estrada',
