   'advanced',
   'full-body',
   array['box','running','barbell']::text[],
   'time',
   'Estrada honors Officer Eric Estrada, who served for eight years with the Tremonton Garland Police Department in Tremonton, Utah. He died on Aug. 17, 2025, after responding to a domestic dispute call involving an active shooter, and was fatally wounded while trying to help a wounded fellow officer. He was a dedicated member of CrossFit Antietam.

You start with 100 box step-ups (20 in) wearing a weighted backpack (50 lb / 35 lb). Then you do 3 rounds of an 800 m run, 17 calories on a bike and 25 front squats (185 lb / 135 lb). The step-ups tire your legs before 75 heavy front squats and 2,400 m of running.',
   '[{"name": "Box Step-Ups", "reps": "100", "tip": "Wear the backpack. Stand all the way up on the box and switch legs each rep.", "rx_men": "20 in, 50 lb backpack", "rx_women": "20 in, 35 lb backpack"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Take the backpack off. Hold a pace you can repeat three times."}, {"name": "Air Bike", "reps": "17 cal", "tip": "CrossFit says bike without naming one. Push hard but save your legs for the squats."}, {"name": "Front Squats", "reps": "25", "tip": "Elbows high and chest up. Break into sets of 5 to 8.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "135 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Pace the step-ups, the squats are heavy", "Rack the bar on your shoulders, not your hands", "Break the front squats early"]'::jsonb,
   '["CrossFit lists Estrada without a time cap or scoring line. Most athletes do it for time.", "The backpack is listed only for the step-ups, so take it off before the first run.", "Count the step-ups in blocks of 10 and keep a steady rhythm rather than rushing.", "On the front squats, keep your elbows up so the bar stays on your shoulders and your back stays upright.", "Put the bike and the bar next to each other so the changes are quick."]'::jsonb,
   'Use a lighter backpack or none, and a lower box. Lower the front squats to 115 lb / 75 lb, or to a load you can squat in sets of 5 while tired. Use a rower for 20 calories if you do not have a bike, and cut the run to 400 m if 800 m takes more than about 5 minutes.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Estrada workout?", "answer": "100 box step-ups (20 in) with a weighted backpack (50 lb / 35 lb), then 3 rounds of an 800 m run, 17-calorie bike and 25 front squats (185 lb / 135 lb)."}, {"question": "How many reps are in Estrada?", "answer": "100 step-ups, 2,400 m of running, 51 calories on the bike and 75 front squats."}, {"question": "What kind of bike is used in Estrada?", "answer": "CrossFit just says bike. An air bike is the most common choice, and any bike with a calorie counter works."}, {"question": "Who was Estrada?", "answer": "Officer Eric Estrada of the Tremonton Garland Police Department in Utah. He died on Aug. 17, 2025, after he was fatally wounded while trying to help a wounded fellow officer during an active shooter call."}]'::jsonb,
