   'Lower the clean and jerks to 135 lb / 95 lb, or to a load each partner can lift for a clean single. Replace double-unders with 48 single-unders each, and toes-to-bar with hanging knee raises. If you do not have a partner, do the whole workout alone, and cut to 3 rounds if needed.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Eva Strong workout?", "answer": "With a partner, 5 rounds for time of 24 double-unders each, 19 toes-to-bar total, 2 clean and jerks total (205 lb / 135 lb) and a 400 m run together."}, {"question": "How many reps are in Eva Strong?", "answer": "For the team: 240 double-unders, 95 toes-to-bar and 10 clean and jerks, plus 2,000 m of running for each partner."}, {"question": "Can I do Eva Strong without a partner?", "answer": "Yes. Do all the double-unders, toes-to-bar and clean and jerks yourself and run alone. It is longer and harder, so pick a load you can lift for singles."}, {"question": "Who was Eva Strong?", "answer": "Eva Mireles, 44, a fourth-grade teacher who died on May 24, 2022, while shielding her students from a gunman at Robb Elementary School in Uvalde, Texas."}]'::jsonb,
