   'rounds_reps',
   'Falkel honors U.S. Army Staff Sgt. Chris Falkel, 22, of Highlands Ranch, Colorado, of the 1st Battalion, 3rd Special Forces Group, based at Fort Bragg, North Carolina. He was killed on Aug. 8, 2005, by enemy small-arms fire in Deh Afghan, Afghanistan.

You get 25 minutes to complete as many rounds and reps as possible of 8 handstand push-ups, 8 box jumps (30 in / 24 in) and 1 rope climb to 15 feet. The handstand push-ups and rope climbs both use your shoulders and arms, so they wear you down together. The tall box makes the jumps a real effort too.',
   '[{"name": "Handstand Push-Ups", "reps": "8", "tip": "Head to the floor or mat and arms locked out at the top. Break into small sets early."}, {"name": "Box Jumps", "reps": "8", "tip": "Stand fully on top of the box. Step down to save your legs and Achilles.", "rx_men": "30 in", "rx_women": "24 in"}, {"name": "Rope Climbs", "reps": "1", "tip": "Use a foot lock to save your arms. Climb to 15 feet and come down under control.", "rx_men": "15 ft", "rx_women": "15 ft"}]'::jsonb,
