   'time',
   'Feeks honors Special Warfare Operator Petty Officer 1st Class Patrick D. Feeks, 28, of Edgewater, Maryland, assigned to a Naval Special Warfare unit based on the West Coast. He died on Aug. 16, 2012, in a helicopter crash northeast of Kandahar, Afghanistan, while supporting Operation Enduring Freedom.

You alternate 100 m shuttle sprints and dumbbell squat clean thrusters (65 lb / 45 lb dumbbells) in a ladder of 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14 and 16 reps. That is 72 shuttle sprints, or 7,200 m, and 72 heavy thrusters. The sprints keep stacking up, so the back half of the ladder is a long test of your legs and lungs.',
   '[{"name": "Shuttle Sprints", "reps": "2-4-6-8-10-12-14-16", "tip": "Each sprint is 100 m. Most gyms run 50 m out and 50 m back. Stay low on the turns."}, {"name": "Dumbbell Squat Clean Thrusters", "reps": "2-4-6-8-10-12-14-16", "tip": "Clean both dumbbells into a full squat, then stand and press them overhead in one move.", "rx_men": "65 lb dumbbells", "rx_women": "45 lb dumbbells"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Do not sprint the early rungs all out", "Clean the dumbbells into the squat in one smooth move", "Count the shuttle sprints out loud"]'::jsonb,
   '["CrossFit does not mark out the 100 m shuttle sprint. Most gyms set two lines 50 m apart and count one trip out and back as one sprint.", "Hold a steady pace on the early sets, since there are 72 sprints in total.", "On each thruster, catch the dumbbells on your shoulders in the bottom of the squat and drive straight up into the press.", "Break the bigger thruster sets into small sets, such as 4 or 5, and rest standing with the dumbbells on the floor.", "Use a counter or a friend to track the sprints, because it is easy to lose count."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the dumbbells to 35 lb / 25 lb, or use one dumbbell. Shorten each shuttle sprint to 50 m (25 m out and back). Stop the ladder at 10 or 12 if the full version would take more than about 70 minutes.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Feeks workout?", "answer": "For time: 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14 and 16 rounds of 100 m shuttle sprints, each followed by the same number of dumbbell squat clean thrusters (65 lb / 45 lb dumbbells)."}, {"question": "How many reps are in Feeks?", "answer": "72 shuttle sprints, or 7,200 m, and 72 dumbbell squat clean thrusters."}, {"question": "How is the 100 m shuttle sprint done?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Most athletes run 50 m out and 50 m back for each sprint."}, {"question": "Who was Feeks?", "answer": "Special Warfare Operator Petty Officer 1st Class Patrick D. Feeks, 28, of Edgewater, Maryland. He died on Aug. 16, 2012, in a helicopter crash northeast of Kandahar, Afghanistan, while supporting Operation Enduring Freedom."}]'::jsonb,
