   'time',
   'FERN honors Darryl Fern of the Highlanders, Royal Regiment of Scotland. While deployed with the Aegis PSD working for the U.S. Department of Defense at Camp Ramadi, he was killed by a roadside improvised explosive device on June 12, 2008, in Kut, Iraq.

Wearing a vest (20 lb / 14 lb), you run 2 miles, then do 9 rounds of a 20-calorie row and 20 burpees, then 3 rounds of 30 push-ups, 30 pull-ups and 30 burpees, all within a 60-minute cap. That is 270 burpees, 180 calories of rowing, 90 push-ups and 90 pull-ups. The vest makes the burpees and push-ups far harder, and the cap means you cannot slow down for long.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "2 miles", "tip": "Wear the vest the whole workout. Run at a pace that leaves room for the rest.", "rx_men": "20 lb vest", "rx_women": "14 lb vest"}, {"name": "Row for Calories", "reps": "9 rounds of 20 cal", "tip": "Drive with your legs and hold a steady pace you can repeat nine times."}, {"name": "Burpees", "reps": "9 rounds of 20", "tip": "Step back and step up to save energy in the vest."}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "3 rounds of 30", "tip": "Chest to the floor and arms locked out. Break into sets of 10 or fewer."}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "3 rounds of 30", "tip": "Chin over the bar. Use small sets to save your grip."}, {"name": "Burpees", "reps": "3 rounds of 30", "tip": "Keep moving. Steady burpees beat long rests."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time under the 60-minute cap.',
   '["Do not race the 2-mile run", "Hold one rowing pace for all nine rounds", "Break the push-ups and pull-ups early"]'::jsonb,
   '["CrossFit gives a 60-minute cap but no rule for scoring if you do not finish. Most athletes record the reps they completed at the cap.", "Treat the run as a warm-up pace, since the vest makes the burpees much harder later.", "Find a row pace you can hold for all nine rounds and step off the rower straight into the burpees.", "Break the 30 push-ups and 30 pull-ups into sets of 6 to 10 from the first round.", "Keep an eye on the clock after the rowing block so you know how much time is left."]'::jsonb,
   'Drop the vest or use a lighter one. Shorten the run to 1 mile, cut the rowing block to 6 rounds, and do push-ups from the knees. Replace pull-ups with jumping pull-ups or ring rows. Scale so you can finish inside the 60-minute cap.',
   '[{"question": "What is the FERN workout?", "answer": "With a 60-minute cap, wearing a vest (20 lb / 14 lb): run 2 miles, then 9 rounds of a 20-calorie row and 20 burpees, then 3 rounds of 30 push-ups, 30 pull-ups and 30 burpees."}, {"question": "How many reps are in FERN?", "answer": "2 miles of running, 180 calories of rowing, 270 burpees, 90 push-ups and 90 pull-ups."}, {"question": "What if I do not finish FERN in 60 minutes?", "answer": "CrossFit does not give a capped scoring rule. Most athletes record the reps they completed when the clock hit 60 minutes."}, {"question": "Who was FERN?", "answer": "Darryl Fern of the Highlanders, Royal Regiment of Scotland. He was killed by a roadside improvised explosive device on June 12, 2008, in Kut, Iraq, while deployed with the Aegis PSD working for the U.S. Department of Defense."}]'::jsonb,
